Z||000000||Fiero_Shane||09-01-2001||08:39 PM||||I've heard that the quikest, easiest and cheapest way to gain HP is to istall a turbo. My dad tells me that the engine block won't be able to handle it and i'm trying to comvince him but he still dousn't believe me. Are there any other ways other than a turbo???<P>By the way I have a '84 SE Automatic<P>Thanks   Shane <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-01-2001||08:49 PM||||I'd listen to dear old dad.  Turbos are not that cheap and a 2.5 Iron Duke has more potential engine problems (bad connecting rods)that may be aggivated with a turbo. You'll be stressing out an 18 year old 4 cylinder engine.<P>A bigger engine would gain HP, but 84's weren't made for V6 swaps in mind.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_Shane||09-01-2001||09:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>I'd listen to dear old dad.  Turbos are not that cheap and a 2.5 Iron Duke has more potential engine problems (bad connecting rods)that may be aggivated with a turbo. You'll be stressing out an 18 year old 4 cylinder engine.<P>A bigger engine would gain HP, but 84's weren't made for V6 swaps in mind.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's the whole thing he won;t let me get a V6 or V8   sooo  I gotta suup up the ol' 4 banger  9thanks for the speedy reply bu the way!!)<P>Shane <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||fiero56||09-01-2001||09:14 PM||||If the duke is able to kill itself on its own and give an entire car model a generalization about fires to the public, a turbo on it isn't the best idea. The Duke was never designed for big power, it gives excellent torque for dail commute, and reasonable performance. <P>It would be very possible to blow the works in very short order with a turbo. 18 years of (ab)use doesn't give the engine any added strength either. I wouldn't, but its not my car. I think your dad has the right idea.<P>Another option is nitrous, which for a duke I would also avoid.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||09-01-2001||09:40 PM||||Bend the rules a little. A Quad 4 gives you as much or sometimes more Hp than a 2.8 does stock. Then put a turbo on that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
